{
  "parts": [
    {
      "id": "sun-body",
      "name": {
        "en": "Sun",
        "zh": "太阳"
      },
      "group": "solar-body",
      "summary": {
        "en": "Provides light.",
        "zh": "提供光照。"
      },
      "detail": {
        "en": "The Sun is a star. It lights the sides of Earth and Moon that face it. [S34,S4,S7]\n\nThe model uses a sphere with a mean radius of 695700 km. A warm colour marks it as the light source. Never look directly at the Sun. [S9,S35,S36]",
        "zh": "太阳是恒星，照亮地球和月球朝向它的一侧。[S34,S4,S7]\n\n模型用球体表示太阳，平均半径为695700 km，暖色帮助辨认光源。不要直视太阳。[S9,S35,S36]"
      },
      "clip": false,
      "castShadow": false,
      "mesh": "sun-body",
      "material": {
        "color": "membrane",
        "tint": "#ffffff"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "earth-body",
      "name": {
        "en": "Earth",
        "zh": "地球"
      },
      "group": "earth-system",
      "summary": {
        "en": "Carries the marked observing place.",
        "zh": "让标记地点随地球转动。"
      },
      "detail": {
        "en": "Earth is a planet. As it turns, places enter and leave sunlight, bringing day and night. Its tilted axis helps explain opposite seasonal daylight changes in the two hemispheres. [S4,S3]\n\nThe model Earth has a mean radius of 6371 km. It follows a circular path with a fixed axis direction. Natural Earth coastlines show the continents; the clouds are an illustration, not dated weather. A fixed ring marks Singapore. Neutral grey fill makes the night side readable. [S9,S36]",
        "zh": "地球是行星。各地随自转进入和离开阳光，形成昼夜。倾斜的地轴有助于解释南北半球相反的季节性日长变化。[S4,S3]\n\n模型平均半径为6371 km，沿圆轨道运行，地轴方向固定。大陆轮廓来自Natural Earth；云层是示意，不代表某日天气。固定圆环标出新加坡，用中性灰填光显示夜侧。[S9,S36]"
      },
      "clip": false,
      "castShadow": false,
      "mesh": "earth-body",
      "material": {
        "color": "matte",
        "tint": "#ffffff"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "earth-axis",
      "name": {
        "en": "Earth axis",
        "zh": "地轴"
      },
      "group": "earth-system",
      "summary": {
        "en": "Shows the axis Earth turns about.",
        "zh": "标出地球自转所绕的轴。"
      },
      "detail": {
        "en": "Earth turns about an imaginary line through its poles. This axis tilts about 23.4 degrees from the perpendicular to its orbital plane. It points in nearly the same direction through a year. [S3,S9]\n\nThe line through the model follows Earth’s orientation. Set the tilt to zero to compare a year without axial tilt. [S36]",
        "zh": "地球绕穿过两极的假想线自转。地轴与轨道平面垂线的夹角约23.4度，一年内方向近似不变。[S3,S9]\n\n模型中的线随地球朝向变化。把倾角设为零，可以比较没有地轴倾角的一年。[S36]"
      },
      "clip": false,
      "castShadow": false,
      "primitive": {
        "kind": "cylinder",
        "size": [
          0.015,
          0.015,
          2.7
        ],
        "at": [
          0,
          0,
          0
        ],
        "color": "matte",
        "tint": "token:ink-3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "equator-ring",
      "name": {
        "en": "Equator",
        "zh": "赤道"
      },
      "group": "earth-system",
      "summary": {
        "en": "Divides Earth into north and south.",
        "zh": "把地球分成南北半球。"
      },
      "detail": {
        "en": "The equator divides Earth into northern and southern hemispheres. At opposite latitudes, seasonal daylight changes can be opposite. [S3]\n\nThe ring marks this imaginary line. In the yearly comparison, the distance to the Sun stays fixed while daylight changes. The model does not calculate temperature. [S36]",
        "zh": "赤道把地球分成南北半球。相反纬度的季节性日长变化可以相反。[S3]\n\n圆环标出这条假想线。全年比较中，日地距离固定，白昼长短仍会变化。模型不计算气温。[S36]"
      },
      "clip": false,
      "castShadow": false,
      "primitive": {
        "kind": "torus",
        "size": [
          1.006,
          0.012
        ],
        "at": [
          0,
          0,
          0
        ],
        "color": "matte",
        "tint": "token:ink-3",
        "rotation": [
          90,
          0,
          0
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "observer-marker",
      "name": {
        "en": "Observer",
        "zh": "观察点"
      },
      "group": "earth-system",
      "summary": {
        "en": "Marks the observer’s place on Earth.",
        "zh": "标出地表观察者的位置。"
      },
      "detail": {
        "en": "The marker follows a place on Earth’s surface. The eclipse window shows the Sun and Moon as seen from this point. The phase window looks from Earth’s centre. [S6,S36]\n\nThe Singapore chapter uses a separate 2026 calculation table for 1.3342° N, 103.7357° E, in UTC+8. This chosen reference point is not an official observatory coordinate. The fixed globe ring marks Singapore at this latitude and longitude. The movable observer shares Singapore’s meridian but can use other latitudes in the experiments; its lighting does not follow the table’s dates. [S33,S36]",
        "zh": "标记跟着地球表面的一个地点转动。日食窗从这里看太阳和月球，月相窗则从地心看。[S6,S36]\n\n新加坡一章采用2026年计算表，地点为北纬1.3342°、东经103.7357°，时区UTC+8。这是选定的参考点，不是官方天文台坐标。球面固定圆环标出这个经纬度的新加坡。活动观察点与新加坡同经线，实验中可改纬度；受光画面不随表格日期改变。[S33,S36]"
      },
      "clip": false,
      "castShadow": false,
      "primitive": {
        "kind": "sphere",
        "size": [
          0.025
        ],
        "at": [
          0,
          0,
          0
        ],
        "color": "matte",
        "tint": "token:signal"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "moon-body",
      "name": {
        "en": "Moon",
        "zh": "月球"
      },
      "group": "moon-system",
      "summary": {
        "en": "Reflects sunlight.",
        "zh": "反射太阳光。"
      },
      "detail": {
        "en": "The Moon is Earth’s natural satellite. As it moves, we see different amounts of its sunlit side. That produces ordinary Moon phases. Earth’s shadow causes lunar eclipses instead. [S7,S5]\n\nThe model uses a mean radius of 1737.4 km. The surface uses NASA LROC maria and crater markings with LOLA relief at its true relative height. The phase window looks from Earth’s centre with north up. It shows the lit fraction separately from eclipse dimming. [S8,S6,S36]",
        "zh": "月球是地球的天然卫星。月球移动时，我们看见的受光部分多少改变，形成普通月相。地影造成的则是月食。[S7,S5]\n\n模型平均半径为1737.4 km。表面按NASA LROC资料显示月海与陨坑，LOLA起伏保持真实相对高度。月相窗从地心看，北方朝上。亮部比例与月食遮暗分别显示。[S8,S6,S36]"
      },
      "clip": false,
      "castShadow": false,
      "mesh": "moon-body",
      "material": {
        "color": "matte",
        "tint": "#ffffff"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "near-side-mark",
      "name": {
        "en": "Near-side mark",
        "zh": "近侧标记"
      },
      "group": "moon-system",
      "summary": {
        "en": "Helps us follow the Moon’s turning.",
        "zh": "帮助追踪月球自转。"
      },
      "detail": {
        "en": "The Moon turns once as it orbits Earth once. This keeps nearly the same face towards Earth. The far side also receives sunlight. [S21,S5]\n\nThe real maria pattern and the small mark help you follow the turning; it is not a real crater. Switch synchrony off to hold its direction fixed relative to space. The model leaves out libration, the small real change in how much of the Moon we see. [S21,S36]",
        "zh": "月球公转一周时也自转一周，让近似同一面朝向地球。背面也会受到阳光照射。[S21,S5]\n\n真实月海图案和小标记帮助追踪转动，不是真实陨坑。关掉同步，月球相对太空的朝向就固定了。模型省略天平动，也就是实际可见月面范围的细小变化。[S21,S36]"
      },
      "clip": false,
      "castShadow": false,
      "primitive": {
        "kind": "cylinder",
        "size": [
          0.06,
          0.06,
          0.012
        ],
        "at": [
          0,
          0,
          0
        ],
        "rotation": [
          0,
          0,
          -90
        ],
        "color": "matte",
        "tint": "token:signal"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lunar-track",
      "name": {
        "en": "Lunar track",
        "zh": "月球轨道"
      },
      "group": "moon-system",
      "summary": {
        "en": "Traces the Moon’s path around Earth.",
        "zh": "标出月球绕地球的路线。"
      },
      "detail": {
        "en": "The Moon’s orbital plane tilts about 5.1 degrees from Earth’s orbital plane. Most new and full Moons therefore miss eclipse alignment. [S8,S40]\n\nThis circular guide shows the model path. At zero tilt, the two orbital planes coincide. Chapters hide the guide when it is not needed. [S36]",
        "zh": "月轨道平面与地球轨道平面相差约5.1度，因此多数新月、满月没有达到日月食所需的排列。[S8,S40]\n\n圆形辅助线标出模型路线。倾角为零时，两轨道平面重合。不需要这条线的章节会把它隐藏。[S36]"
      },
      "clip": false,
      "castShadow": false,
      "primitive": {
        "kind": "box",
        "size": [
          0.001,
          0.001,
          0.001
        ],
        "at": [
          0,
          0,
          0
        ],
        "color": "matte",
        "tint": "token:ink-3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "earth-track",
      "name": {
        "en": "Earth track",
        "zh": "地球轨道"
      },
      "group": "orbital-guides",
      "summary": {
        "en": "Traces Earth’s path around the Sun.",
        "zh": "标出地球绕太阳的路线。"
      },
      "detail": {
        "en": "Earth travels around the Sun. Its tilted axis keeps nearly the same direction, so the hemispheres take turns leaning towards sunlight. [S3,S4]\n\nThe model path is a circle with radius 149597870.7 km, the defined astronomical unit. Earth’s real distance from the Sun varies. This circle explains positions without predicting dated events. [S10,S3,S36]",
        "zh": "地球绕太阳运行，倾斜的地轴方向近似不变，两半球便轮流倾向太阳。[S3,S4]\n\n模型路线是半径149597870.7 km的圆，采用天文单位的定义值。真实日地距离会变化，这个圆用来解释位置，不预测具体日期的天象。[S10,S3,S36]"
      },
      "clip": false,
      "castShadow": false,
      "primitive": {
        "kind": "box",
        "size": [
          0.001,
          0.001,
          0.001
        ],
        "at": [
          0,
          0,
          0
        ],
        "color": "matte",
        "tint": "token:ink-3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "orbital-plane",
      "name": {
        "en": "Orbital plane",
        "zh": "轨道平面"
      },
      "group": "orbital-guides",
      "summary": {
        "en": "Provides a reference for tilt angles.",
        "zh": "提供测量倾角的参考面。"
      },
      "detail": {
        "en": "This is Earth’s orbital plane. Measure axial tilt from a line perpendicular to it. Measure lunar orbital tilt between this plane and the Moon’s orbital plane. [S3,S8,S9]\n\nThe wire outline helps show the plane clearly. Set lunar tilt to zero and the two orbital planes coincide. [S36]",
        "zh": "这是地球轨道平面。地轴倾角从它的垂线量起，月轨道倾角则在它与月球轨道平面之间量起。[S3,S8,S9]\n\n线框帮助显示这个平面。月轨道倾角设为零时，两轨道平面重合。[S36]"
      },
      "clip": false,
      "castShadow": false,
      "primitive": {
        "kind": "box",
        "size": [
          0.001,
          0.001,
          0.001
        ],
        "at": [
          0,
          0,
          0
        ],
        "color": "matte",
        "tint": "token:ink-3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-line",
      "name": {
        "en": "Node line",
        "zh": "轨道交线"
      },
      "group": "orbital-guides",
      "summary": {
        "en": "Shows where the orbital planes meet.",
        "zh": "标出两轨道平面的交线。"
      },
      "detail": {
        "en": "The Moon’s orbit crosses Earth’s orbital plane at two nodes. A new or full Moon near a node can line up for an eclipse. [S40]\n\nThe line marks where the planes meet. At zero tilt, the planes overlap completely, so there is no single crossing line to show. The window explains why the line is hidden. [S36]",
        "zh": "月球轨道在两个交点穿过地球轨道平面。新月或满月接近交点时，才可能排成日月食。[S40]\n\n这条线标出平面相交的位置。倾角为零时，平面完全重合，没有唯一交线，窗口会说明隐藏原因。[S36]"
      },
      "clip": false,
      "castShadow": false,
      "primitive": {
        "kind": "box",
        "size": [
          0.001,
          0.001,
          0.001
        ],
        "at": [
          0,
          0,
          0
        ],
        "color": "matte",
        "tint": "token:ink-3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "light-ray-guide",
      "name": {
        "en": "Sunward rays",
        "zh": "太阳光线"
      },
      "group": "orbital-guides",
      "summary": {
        "en": "Shows the direction towards the Sun.",
        "zh": "标出朝向太阳的方向。"
      },
      "detail": {
        "en": "The guide points from Earth towards the Sun and marks the boundary between light and dark. Compare the surface marker with the lit half of Earth. [S3,S36]\n\nThe lines show directions and the light boundary. They are drawn guides, not visible beams in space or measurements of light’s travel time. [S36]",
        "zh": "辅助线从地球指向太阳，并标出明暗交界。比较地表标记与地球受光半面的位置。[S3,S36]\n\n线条表示方向和明暗边界，不是真空中可见的光束，也不测量光传播时间。[S36]"
      },
      "clip": false,
      "castShadow": false,
      "primitive": {
        "kind": "box",
        "size": [
          0.001,
          0.001,
          0.001
        ],
        "at": [
