        "tint": "token:ink-3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "scale-ruler",
      "name": {
        "en": "Centre distance ruler",
        "zh": "中心距标尺"
      },
      "group": "orbital-guides",
      "summary": {
        "en": "Compares centre distance and surface gap.",
        "zh": "比较中心距与表面间隙。"
      },
      "detail": {
        "en": "The ruler joins Earth’s and the Moon’s centres. With Earth 10 mm across, their centres are about 302 mm apart and their surfaces about 295 mm apart. [S8,S9,S36]\n\nThe ruler appears in the true-scale comparison, where sizes and distances share one scale. It is hidden in views that enlarge bodies and shorten gaps separately. [S36]",
        "zh": "标尺连接地月球心。地球直径画成10 mm时，两球中心相距约302 mm，表面相隔约295 mm。[S8,S9,S36]\n\n标尺只在大小和距离采用同一比例的真尺度对照中显示。在分别放大球体、缩短间距的画面中，标尺隐藏。[S36]"
      },
      "clip": false,
      "castShadow": false,
      "primitive": {
